# TEARS

**AUDITOR LACRIMARUM**

*The Listener of Tears*

**Reactive Relics — Experimental Device**

TEARS is an experimental sensing relic developed within the Reactive Relics instrumentarium.

Its purpose is simple and impossible:

**to listen to tears.**

The device explores the transformation of liquid, body and ritual gesture into electronic signal. A drop becomes an event; the event becomes a signal; the signal becomes a response.

---

## CONCEPT

TEARS takes inspiration from the long religious tradition surrounding the tears of the Virgin Mary and the figure of the **Mater Lacrimosa** — the sorrowful mother who weeps.

Within the fictional mythology of Reactive Relics, TEARS becomes a technological relic dedicated to detecting and interpreting these traces.

It does not simply measure water.

It **listens for tears**.

---

## THE AUDITOR

The name **AUDITOR LACRIMARUM** can be read as:

> *The Listener of Tears*

The device therefore adopts the character of an instrument belonging to an unknown liturgy: part sensor, part reliquary and part listening apparatus.

The technical action of detecting a liquid event becomes a ritual act of listening.

